From a535b2dfc286dfc1454d4c3a51a99c225a37e0c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:21:58 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] feat(post): Tormach PathPilot post and 770MX machine;
 machine units reach posts

A Tormach PathPilot (LinuxCNC-dialect) 3-axis post and a Tormach 770MX
machine file in inches, from Tormach's and LinuxCNC's public docs.
The post writes no % fence and no O word, states G91.1 and a G64 P
tolerance, a G30 before every tool change, G43 H from the tool table,
dwell P in seconds, G84 tapping, a belt-range comment for speeds only
one 770 belt range serves, refuses tool numbers outside 1-1000, and
ends Z-up, G30, M30 as PathPilot's own programs do.

Machine files could already state inches, but the parser dropped the
unit after scaling to mm. Machine gains `units` (Some("inch") when the
file states inches; skipped when None, so project files are unchanged),
and the post mirror and script_props expose it as `machine.units`; the
Tormach post writes G20 and inch values from it. Other posts ignore it.

Refs #131

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
