From a02b1ed24bf384b7afdef89ca6c3b3660a48eb3f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:33:47 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] fix(post): lift Z before the G30 at every Tormach tool
 change

A bare G30 can move X, Y and Z together. Between tools PathPilot's own
Conversational programs lift Z first, then G30; the post now writes
G53 G0 Z0 (top of Z travel, machine coordinates) before the G30 that
precedes every T.. M6, the same Z-first order its program end uses.

The old "G30 before M6" check ran only over golden streams with no tool
change, so it never fired; a two-tool test now pins the sequence.

Refs #131

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
