Subject: [PATCH 4/6] fix(post): position X Y with Z up before the first
 Tormach move

X and Y are unknown at program start and after every G30, so the first
move after a tool change started wherever the table happened to be; the
PathPilot Hub simulator (v2.14.4) flags it: "Axis XY not specified by
this or previous motions, end point will depend on current position".
That move is now preceded by a G0 to its X Y alone at the current, Z-up
height (a rapid's target, a feed or arc's stream start point, a cycle's
first hole), PathPilot's own XY-first order, and only then does Z come
down. Each Tormach golden gains that one line.

